Change(genesis='66602cd0dec37d58d03eec9518ca805a7ac38ea912d2b0c366a0b67b4b9f50b6', deps=(), event=Decided(decision='addressnotidentity', at=datetime(2026, 10, 9, 0, 0, 0), actor='assistant', title='An address is not an identity: every request, loopback included, asks whois; proxies and foreign Hosts are refused', body="The tailnet is SHARED, so the bind address is half the access control: the gate asks tailscaled's local API (a unix socket, not the CLI) who owns each peer and admits `web.viewers` only (Tailscale LOGINS, not actors); unresolved 403, STATIC FILES gated too. AN ADDRESS IS NOT AN IDENTITY (2026-10-09): nothing is exempt, so loopback asks whois like any peer and a `tailscale serve` or proxy on the box reads nothing; a request carrying a proxy's header (`gate::PROXY_HEADERS`) or a `Host` other than `app_url`'s (`gate::Door`, against DNS rebinding) is refused before the lookup. Plain http listens on loopback alone (`serve::listening::Listening`), `serve` refuses an `app_url` whose port it does not bind (`gate::door_at`), and `serve-web.sh` refuses to start without the tailnet address and the certificate, or beside a `tailscale serve` of its port. Every answer carries `serve::POLICY` (the CSP: own-origin scripts, workers and wasm, no inline script, inline style attributes alone because typst lays out with them, no base, form or frame) and every API answer `no-store`, a JSON read with a weak `ETag` of its bytes (`serve::validated`; the page keeps its last answers and sends the tag, and a 304 is that answer again), but an object's literal asked for by its name (`…/content?hashes=`, 2026-10-21, `docs/LAZYSYNC-PLAN-2026-10-21.md`), which never changes and is sent `private, immutable` (`reply::Immutable`); a refusal of one is `no-store`.", rationale="Decided 2026-10-09; an object's literal is immutable by name since 2026-10-21 (docs/LAZYSYNC-PLAN-2026-10-21.md).", supersedes=()))